          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Sometimes. If the slab is sound, level and drains well, thin pavers can be installed over it with a bedding layer and proper drainage at the edges. Cracked or heaving slabs make poor bases, since their movement will show through. Raising the surface height can also cause problems at doors and steps. Many installers prefer to remove the slab and build a proper base."
